WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.251
On stage you want the picture big and the controls close.

2
00:00:04.251 --> 00:00:06.993
The Performance layout maximizes the output.

3
00:00:07.961 --> 00:00:11.734
Press H for the HUD: frame rate, source and render size.

4
00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:13.486
Press it again to hide it.

5
00:00:13.944 --> 00:00:15.616
Back to the default layout.

6
00:00:15.616 --> 00:00:20.322
Bracket keys flip between the panel tabs, and slash jumps to the search box.

7
00:00:21.455 --> 00:00:24.577
The Performance section trades quality for speed.

8
00:00:24.577 --> 00:00:28.145
Battery caps the frame rate and drops the heavy effects.

9
00:00:28.145 --> 00:00:31.012
Render Scale changes the internal resolution.

10
00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:37.781
Virtual Camera sets a fixed output resolution, like full HD for a projector, letterboxed to fit.

11
00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:45.103
Fly mode turns the camera into a free-flying ship: W A S D to move, the mouse to steer, Shift to boost.

12
00:00:45.564 --> 00:00:51.516
For syncing with video, the Timeline can count in timecode, frames, or samples instead of bars.

13
00:00:51.980 --> 00:01:01.430
And for two screens, Window, Pop Out Output sends the picture to its own window, ready to go fullscreen on a projector, while the controls stay on your laptop.

14
00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.162
Last lesson: putting it all together.
